@title Shipment webhook delivery
@subtitle How Parcelwise delivers shipment webhooks to merchants
@author Parcelwise integrations docs
@date 2026-10-05

!! **Responses slower than 10 seconds count as failures.** Your endpoint must answer within 10 s, or the delivery is retried, even if you processed the event.

## Delivery sequence

diagram hook sequence title="Webhook delivery with one retry"
hook: order "Order Service" svc
hook: bus "Event Bus" queue
hook: worker "Delivery Worker" svc
hook: merchant "Merchant Endpoint" ext
hook: dlq "Dead Letter Queue" queue
hook: order -> bus : publish order.shipped
hook: bus -> worker : deliver event
hook: worker -> merchant : POST /webhooks, signed, 10 s timeout
hook: merchant --> worker : 503 Service Unavailable
hook: worker -> bus : requeue with 1 minute delay
hook: bus -> worker : deliver event, attempt 2
hook: worker -> merchant : POST /webhooks
hook: merchant --> worker : 200 OK
hook: worker -> bus : acknowledge
hook: opt "merchant never recovers"
hook: worker -> dlq : park after attempt 6
hook: end

## Retry schedule

table = attempt,delay after previous failure; 1,Immediate; 2,1 minute; 3,5 minutes; 4,30 minutes; 5,2 hours; 6,12 hours

After attempt 6 fails, the event is parked in the Dead Letter Queue.

## Good to know

- Every request carries an `X-Parcelwise-Signature` header: an HMAC-SHA256 of the request body. Verify it before trusting the event.
- Events can arrive out of order. Compare the sequence number before applying an update.
- Parked events are kept for 14 days and can be replayed from the dashboard.
